psx_patches/0021: System 573 GPU = 2 MB VRAM (1024 rows) -- widen Y to 10 bits end-to-end.

The 573's CXD8561Q GPU drives 2 MB of VRAM (1024 rows x 1024 x 16bpp); the vendored
consumer-PSX core implements 1 MB (512 rows) and truncates every Y to 9 bits. Effects
fixed here (all field conventions cross-checked against MAME psxgpu, gputype 2):
 1. Unscissored engines (A0 cpu2vram / 80 vram2vram / C0 vram2cpu / 02 fill) parsed
    Y/h as fifo_data(24:16): an upload to (x,512..1023) dropped Y bit 9 and WRAPPED
    onto y-512, overwriting the visible lower half (the boot font-atlas corruption:
    cols 14-15 of each 16-word block survive, 0-13 get foreign upper-half data).
    Now: dst/src Y = (25:16) 10-bit, sizes 0x400-defaulting (MAME masks Y & 1023).
 2. Scissored renders to y>=512 were culled: E3/E4 drawing-area Y now (19:10) 10-bit
    (MAME gputype 2: y=(w>>10)&1023), drawer y plumbing + pixel pipeline y 9->10 bit.
 3. Texture side: texpage Y-base bit 11 = +512 (MAME: ty=((tp&0x10)<<4)|((tp&0x800)>>2));
    CLUT row 10-bit, attr bit 31 = CLUT Y bit 9 (MAME: cluty=(attr>>6)&0x3ff). The
    texture cache TAG gains the new address bit (no aliasing between Y-base halves).
 4. Address mapping: VRAM rows 512-1023 live at vram_ADDR(27:20) = x"08" (+8 MB),
    keeping the existing 9-bit row layout inside the page. Pages 0x01/0x02 (memcards),
    0x03 (SPU), 0x04-0x07 (videoout framebuffers) stay untouched. EVERY VRAM path
    applies the mapping at the single composition site in gpu.vhd (engine writes via
    the +1-bit fifoOut address, all reads via the widened shared reqVRAMYPos).
 5. Scanout (videoout) is BIT-IDENTICAL: its 9-bit request Y is zero-padded into the
    OR-mux, so display fetches stay page-0/page-4 exactly as before. GP1(05) display
    base Y stays 9-bit (a y>=512 display base is not displayable -- documented limit;
    the 573 boot/games display from the lower half).
Savestate compat: drawingArea Top/Bottom move from ss words 4/5 bits (24:16) to
(25:16); bit 25 was unused in both words, so OLD savestates load unchanged (bit 25
reads 0). No other savestate field moves. The 480i-framebuffer-hack write heuristics
are gated to page-0 writes (upper-half writes no longer alias into them). render24
(consumer 24-bit mode, OFF on the 573) keeps its page-4 second-write behavior.
